Summary (non-binding -- the full terms below control)
-----------------------------------------------------

Scorium is "source-available" and "community-source", not open source as
defined by the Open Source Initiative (OSI). In plain language:

  - You may read, run, audit, and learn from the source.
  - You may use Scorium for personal, educational, hobby, and local
    noncommercial purposes.
  - You may modify it privately for learning, testing, and experimentation.
  - You may fork on GitHub to prepare a contribution back to the project.
  - You may NOT use Scorium commercially without written permission.
  - You may NOT sell it, redistribute it, publish it to a package registry,
    ship independent binaries, or maintain a renamed public fork without
    written permission.
  - The name "Scorium" and its branding are controlled by Fiw Labs.

For commercial use, see COMMERCIAL.md. For contribution-focused permissions
beyond this license, see CONTRIBUTION_PERMISSION.md. For contributor grants,
see CONTRIBUTOR_TERMS.md.


